WEBVTT

01:42.760 --> 01:47.770
In an emergency session held on
the 3rd, the World Health Organization

01:47.770 --> 01:52.770
classified ACIS, or "Medousa," as an
infectious disease of the highest level.

01:52.770 --> 01:56.780
Despite the inability to identify
a cause, this decision was made

01:56.780 --> 02:01.780
under the assumption that global unrest
could break unless measures are taken.

02:01.780 --> 02:04.790
The WHO has issued a statement
requesting nations worldwide

02:04.790 --> 02:09.780
to provide physical safeguards
and disclose detailed information.

02:11.130 --> 02:16.800
...We learned that the body,
once infected with ACIS,

02:16.800 --> 02:20.970
produces this chemical
substance in large quantities.

02:20.970 --> 02:23.970
So, by measuring the amount
of this substance in the body,

02:23.970 --> 02:27.380
we're now able to determine
if someone is infected or not!

02:27.380 --> 02:32.850
However, the cause and any
possible cures remain unknown.

02:32.850 --> 02:38.250
The first stage after infection is an
incubation period lasting 30 to 60 days,

02:38.250 --> 02:44.160
followed by a 12-hour second stage
that leads to a petrified-like state.

02:44.160 --> 02:47.160
The fatality rate is 100%.

02:47.160 --> 02:52.100
Cruel numbers continue to be
the only information we have.

02:53.900 --> 02:57.210
Our nation's borders are
being flooded with refugees

02:57.210 --> 03:01.110
hoping to flee the
country to avoid infection.

03:01.110 --> 03:05.110
The government has augmented
security forces along the borders

03:05.110 --> 03:08.510
and is also looking into
activating the National Guard.

03:10.450 --> 03:16.190
A statement was issued that justifies the
aerial bombings conducted on the 20th

03:16.190 --> 03:19.760
as a preemptive strike necessary
for the sake of national defense.

03:19.760 --> 03:24.390
The U.N. Security Council held an
emergency meeting regarding this...

03:25.930 --> 03:29.940
The drastic decline in labor has resulted
in closed factories and businesses,

03:29.940 --> 03:33.410
causing tremendous earnings
drops across the board.

03:33.410 --> 03:35.410
Stock prices continue to plummet,

03:35.410 --> 03:41.140
with the index down a
record 47% from last year.

03:43.050 --> 03:45.920
The U.N. Security Council
has unanimously voted in favor

03:45.920 --> 03:47.920
of declaring a state of emergency.

03:47.920 --> 03:51.480
Special committee
meetings are being held...

03:53.290 --> 03:57.230
Mr. Vega, CEO of the major
chemical manufacturer Venus Gate,

03:57.230 --> 04:01.340
announced a shocking plan
at a company press conference.

04:01.340 --> 04:04.910
Given the unprecedented
crisis that now faces us,

04:04.910 --> 04:09.080
I have decided it is time for this
corporation to fulfill its duty to society

04:09.080 --> 04:12.080
and unveil the top-secret
project we have been working on.

04:12.080 --> 04:16.640
That project is "cold sleep."

04:18.090 --> 04:22.090
So you're saying it's highly
likely that Medousa... no, ACIS...

04:22.090 --> 04:25.790
is an act of bioterrorism
perpetrated by Venus Gate?

04:25.790 --> 04:26.960
Yes.

04:26.960 --> 04:29.430
That sounds a little far-fetched.

04:29.430 --> 04:33.530
Venus Gate is one of the nation's
largest chemical manufacturers

04:33.530 --> 04:36.870
and even owns top-notch
medical-related corporations,

04:36.870 --> 04:40.940
yet it hasn't announced any
new products for several years now.

04:40.940 --> 04:45.110
Meanwhile, they've been collecting
biological samples all over the world

04:45.110 --> 04:47.620
and preserving them in their facility.

04:47.620 --> 04:50.490
And this is their cold sleep facility?

04:50.490 --> 04:52.190
On the outside, yes.

04:52.190 --> 04:57.560
On the inside, it's more like
a heavily-secured fortress.

04:57.560 --> 05:00.560
But, as you say, we're talking about

05:00.560 --> 05:03.730
one of the biggest
chemical manufacturers here.

05:03.730 --> 05:08.040
They've donated huge amounts of
money to each successive ruling party.

05:08.040 --> 05:13.540
Venus Gate's biggest shareholder
is a cult proclaiming the end of times.

05:13.540 --> 05:17.380
So you're saying this facility
is a sort of "Noah's Ark"?

05:17.380 --> 05:19.380
And Mr. Vega, the CEO,

05:19.380 --> 05:24.590
was once a lead scientific
investigator for the Russian MIA.

05:24.590 --> 05:28.560
However, at some point
he began uttering absurdities

05:28.560 --> 05:31.560
and was eventually
relieved of his position.

05:31.560 --> 05:34.030
What sort of absurdities?

05:34.030 --> 05:39.670
"I've been chosen.
I've found the path to God."

05:39.670 --> 05:42.370
The reduced metabolic
rate during cold sleep

05:42.370 --> 05:44.910
can slow the progress of illnesses.

05:44.910 --> 05:51.450
Our research has shown that
this holds true for ACIS as well.

05:51.450 --> 05:55.720
A patient can now relax
in an indefinitely long sleep

05:55.720 --> 05:59.290
and travel toward the day in
the future when a cure is discovered!

05:59.290 --> 06:01.290
We haven't a moment to waste.

06:01.290 --> 06:06.590
Intel analysis suggests it is likely
that the cold sleep center's activation

06:06.590 --> 06:12.570
will also signal their next action...
a second terrorist act, in other words.

06:12.570 --> 06:17.810
We may never get another chance
to go on the offensive or defensive.

06:17.810 --> 06:20.110
Have you consulted
the president about this?

06:20.110 --> 06:23.710
The president passed away at 1206 hours.

06:23.710 --> 06:26.200
The cause of death was Medousa.

06:28.080 --> 06:30.790
I ask for your decision.

06:30.790 --> 06:35.290
Unfortunately, our facility only
has enough room for 160 people.

06:35.290 --> 06:37.730
Should the number of
applicants exceed that number,

06:37.730 --> 06:41.830
a lottery system will be employed.

06:41.830 --> 06:44.900
All right.
What is this operation's name?

06:44.900 --> 06:48.390
"Sleeping Beauty."

06:49.170 --> 06:55.680
Once upon a time, there was a
king and queen who were very close.

06:55.680 --> 06:58.950
However, they were unhappy

06:58.950 --> 07:04.690
because they couldn't have a child,
however hard they tried.

07:04.690 --> 07:09.620
Not even the doctors and
sorcerers could do anything to help.

07:09.620 --> 07:11.990
Even the royal subjects
and citizens were heartbroken

07:11.990 --> 07:15.160
and prayed to Heaven every day.

07:15.160 --> 07:23.040
One day, while the queen was bathing,
a frog appeared and said to her,

07:23.040 --> 07:29.880
"Your wish will come true.
Heaven shall bless you with a child."

07:29.880 --> 07:33.210
It was truly mysterious.

07:33.210 --> 07:35.220
And... wouldn't you know it...

07:35.220 --> 07:41.290
the queen gave birth to an
adorable little girl, just as predicted.

07:41.290 --> 07:46.560
Overjoyed, the king
decided to hold a celebration.

07:46.560 --> 07:52.230
Not only the king's family came;
many others were invited to the castle,

07:52.230 --> 07:55.200
some from the kingdom
and some from beyond.

07:55.200 --> 07:58.540
Special visitors arrived as well.

08:00.980 --> 08:04.670
Look, Kasumi! The castle!

08:06.310 --> 08:08.850
Say, Shizuku...

08:08.850 --> 08:10.920
I think we should go home after all...

08:10.920 --> 08:14.660
Sheesh... How many
times have you said that now?

08:14.660 --> 08:17.590
It'll be all right!
There's nothing to worry about!

08:17.590 --> 08:19.330
That isn't what I...

08:19.330 --> 08:23.060
The thirteen witches had special powers,

08:23.060 --> 08:28.600
and their celebratory words promised
a happy future for the little princess.

08:28.600 --> 08:32.700
That's "Sleeping Beauty," isn't it?

08:39.710 --> 08:43.750
No, you lost all custody rights long ago.

08:43.750 --> 08:46.750
I felt he deserved the right to enter,

08:46.750 --> 08:50.850
so I applied for him and he was chosen.

08:53.060 --> 08:55.790
A new stage!

08:59.600 --> 09:02.040
Back off.

09:02.040 --> 09:05.770
It's obvious you're gonna ask,
"How are you feeling?"

09:05.770 --> 09:09.230
just like you types always do.

09:11.980 --> 09:15.450
Fine. Get the scenery instead.

09:15.450 --> 09:16.550
Ready?

09:16.550 --> 09:19.620
What, you ain't gonna tape us?!

09:19.620 --> 09:23.060
I went outta my way
to join your little picnic, too!

09:23.060 --> 09:25.390
I don't even get a commemorative photo?!

09:25.390 --> 09:26.630
Pipe down!

09:26.630 --> 09:28.250
Oww!

09:32.330 --> 09:35.840
However, as luck would have it,

09:35.840 --> 09:42.740
there were only twelve special
gold saucers for the special guests.

09:42.740 --> 09:47.010
The thirteenth flock is in the coop.

11:09.530 --> 11:14.040
Welcome to the Cold Sleep Center!

11:14.040 --> 11:16.540
BNN News! How do you feel?!

11:16.540 --> 11:18.010
Oh! BNN News!

11:18.010 --> 11:21.500
Excuse me! We're with BNN News!
How do you feel?

11:28.180 --> 11:30.850
- Listen, Shizuku...
- Oh, give me a break!

11:30.850 --> 11:32.720
Excuse me!

11:32.720 --> 11:35.720
I'm with BNN News! How do you feel?!

11:35.720 --> 11:37.850
Don't bother us!

11:38.860 --> 11:42.530
Patients with companions,
please come this way.

11:42.530 --> 11:44.730
More scenery?

11:44.730 --> 11:46.430
Umm...

11:46.430 --> 11:49.570
Yes! How do you feel?!

11:49.570 --> 11:53.060
I feel great!

12:25.070 --> 12:27.340
- Are you getting this?!
- You bet I am!

12:56.500 --> 12:57.510
Welcome!

12:57.510 --> 12:59.940
Nice to meet you.

12:59.940 --> 13:01.530
C'mon.

13:02.210 --> 13:06.940
Please check in at the great hall.

13:17.560 --> 13:19.620
Next, please.

13:25.330 --> 13:29.870
Welcome to the Cold Sleep Capsule Center.

13:29.870 --> 13:34.380
Selectee Kasumi Ishiki and her
companion, Shizuku Ishiki, correct?

13:34.380 --> 13:36.010
Yes.

13:36.010 --> 13:40.350
Please stick out your left hand.

13:40.350 --> 13:45.150
Your ID code is KHM050.

13:45.150 --> 13:48.920
Only people wearing these
bracelets can go further inside.

13:48.920 --> 13:52.560
Make sure you always keep it on.

13:52.560 --> 13:53.260
Umm...

13:53.260 --> 13:57.100
Orientation will be held in
the chapel in thirty minutes.

13:57.100 --> 13:58.870
Please hurry.

13:58.870 --> 14:02.740
Follow me. I'll show you the way.

14:02.740 --> 14:04.410
Shizuku...

14:04.410 --> 14:07.910
It's okay! I'll just take a little tour!

14:07.910 --> 14:11.050
When the eleventh witch
finished giving her blessing,

14:11.050 --> 14:14.450
the thirteenth witch,
convinced she was being left out,

14:14.450 --> 14:17.690
interrupted the twelfth witch and said,

14:17.690 --> 14:23.260
"On her 15th birthday, the princess
will be pierced by a spindle and die."

14:23.260 --> 14:27.460
They were the words of a terrible curse.

14:28.730 --> 14:30.720
Now, then...

14:32.600 --> 14:38.640
With that general explanation out
of the way, are there any questions?

14:38.640 --> 14:40.210
I have one.

14:40.210 --> 14:41.380
Go ahead.

14:41.380 --> 14:46.480
What if while we're asleep, umm...
I know I shouldn't say this, but...

14:46.480 --> 14:47.650
Go right ahead.

14:47.650 --> 14:51.250
What if the Medousa virus
kills the people working here?

14:51.250 --> 14:55.760
I see. I understand your concern very well.

14:55.760 --> 14:58.330
Allow me to introduce Alice,

14:58.330 --> 15:03.430
the greatest, most cutting-edge
centralized management control system!

15:03.430 --> 15:06.430
This system has been
designed to perpetually maintain

15:06.430 --> 15:09.440
not only the underground
cold sleep capsule room,

15:09.440 --> 15:13.270
but this castle and all
peripheral equipment as well.

15:13.270 --> 15:16.510
Calculations show
that its service life will last

15:16.510 --> 15:20.450
over 100 years!

15:20.450 --> 15:22.420
100 years...

15:22.420 --> 15:27.760
However, the twelfth
witch followed by saying,

15:27.760 --> 15:30.860
"I cannot lift the curse
placed upon the princess,

15:30.860 --> 15:33.490
but I can put her
to sleep for 100 years instead.

15:33.490 --> 15:35.760
The poison should be gone by then.

15:35.760 --> 15:40.200
You need only entrust her
to one with a sound heart."

15:41.970 --> 15:47.340
There are also the bracelets you were
given when you entered the facility.

15:47.340 --> 15:51.880
Alice has been programmed
to protect everyone wearing one.

15:51.880 --> 15:55.950
Even as we speak, she is
monitoring your health, mental state,

15:55.950 --> 15:59.280
and immediate circumstances.

16:02.990 --> 16:08.030
Alice is also an enormous
databank that stores full backups

16:08.030 --> 16:12.970
of not only your personal
information, but detailed bio-data

16:12.970 --> 16:15.970
and genetic information as well.

16:15.970 --> 16:17.970
Please leave everything to Alice

16:17.970 --> 16:20.980
and enter your sleep with an easy mind.

16:20.980 --> 16:22.540
I have a question!

16:22.540 --> 16:24.080
Yes?

16:24.080 --> 16:26.010
I'm with BNN News.

16:26.010 --> 16:29.880
Will people dream during cold sleep?

16:29.880 --> 16:35.090
That's an interesting
question, and a good one.

16:35.090 --> 16:40.560
Never fear. Alice can
even control your dreams.

16:40.560 --> 16:44.870
Specifically, the minute electrical
currents generated by the brain

16:44.870 --> 16:48.270
are converted into patterns,
modified via proprietary algorithms,

16:48.270 --> 16:52.910
then fed back into...

16:52.910 --> 16:55.710
Well, technical jargon aside,

16:55.710 --> 17:03.180
you will enjoy soothing dreams on
your journey to the world of the future.

17:03.180 --> 17:05.020
Well, it's almost time to go,

17:05.020 --> 17:09.220
but there's one last thing to mention.

17:09.220 --> 17:14.290
The bracelets you're wearing
allow Alice to look after you,

17:14.290 --> 17:16.760
but they also serve another purpose.

17:16.760 --> 17:21.600
This white area in the center
is a symptom indicator.

17:21.600 --> 17:24.740
If, by some chance, your
Medousa infection enters its second stage,

17:24.740 --> 17:27.980
this area will turn black...

17:27.980 --> 17:29.580
No!

17:29.580 --> 17:33.580
No! No! No!

17:33.580 --> 17:35.880
No! No!

17:35.880 --> 17:39.610
Doctor to the chapel immediately.

17:48.230 --> 17:52.070
It's not too late yet...

17:52.070 --> 17:57.970
I apologize for the commotion.
It's now time to go.

18:02.680 --> 18:05.450
100 years in a castle...

18:05.450 --> 18:08.650
It's almost exactly like "Sleeping Beauty."

18:08.650 --> 18:12.920
Even you're talking that way?

18:12.920 --> 18:17.160
In the fairytale her family
and subjects go to sleep too...

18:17.160 --> 18:19.180
But, I'm...

18:21.330 --> 18:26.530
I guess there isn't a God.
There are only evil sorcerers.

18:26.530 --> 18:28.870
- Kasumi...
- Don't you agree?!

18:28.870 --> 18:32.110
Mom and Dad died, and
now I'm going to lose you too!

18:32.110 --> 18:34.310
- Kasumi!
- We promised!

18:34.310 --> 18:39.950
We promised we'd always stick together!
That we'd live together!

18:39.950 --> 18:44.350
Kasumi. It's not set in stone that I'll die.

18:53.630 --> 18:57.560
I'm sorry. I'm not thinking right.

19:00.700 --> 19:05.070
Kasumi. Here's Part 2 of our promise!

19:05.070 --> 19:08.240
I'll always be waiting for you,

19:08.240 --> 19:13.050
so come look for me
as soon as you wake up.

19:13.050 --> 19:14.750
I'm sure we'll meet again.

19:14.750 --> 19:17.680
Miracles only happen
where there's a wish.

19:17.680 --> 19:22.060
It was because of the twelfth witch's
wish that the princess survived!

19:22.060 --> 19:24.720
Wishing will make a miracle happen?

19:26.760 --> 19:29.230
Yes! It will!

19:42.610 --> 19:45.200
I've decided. I!

19:47.610 --> 19:49.950
Personal belongings are not
allowed inside the capsules.

19:49.950 --> 19:52.350
We will hold on to
them in the center's vault

19:52.350 --> 19:54.860
and return them to you after
coming out of cold sleep.

19:54.860 --> 19:59.690
What the hell?!
This is no different from the slammer!

19:59.690 --> 20:04.530
Only glasses and hearing aids
are allowed inside the capsules.

20:05.600 --> 20:07.770
Will you really give it back?

20:07.770 --> 20:10.360
We'll take full responsibility.

20:12.810 --> 20:14.710
Mrs. Turner!

20:16.410 --> 20:18.910
It's a memento of my late husband...

20:18.910 --> 20:20.640
I'm sorry, but...

20:22.120 --> 20:24.280
I...

20:29.990 --> 20:38.800
Yes... I'm sure that each time
I look into the mirror I'll think of you...

20:38.800 --> 20:44.300
I'll remember my sister
who looked just like me...

20:44.300 --> 20:50.110
And when I'm twenty,
I'll meet the twenty year old you...

20:51.950 --> 20:53.740
Oww!

20:54.080 --> 21:00.020
And when I'm forty,
I'll meet the forty year old you...

21:26.980 --> 21:30.150
I welcome you all once more!

21:30.150 --> 21:32.690
This is the final stop in our center

21:32.690 --> 21:35.480
and the first stop toward the future!

21:36.960 --> 21:40.830
It is time for Noah's Ark to depart!

21:40.830 --> 21:46.630
May your future... and the future
of humankind... be a glorious one!

22:12.090 --> 22:16.830
Please step in. Oh, you can
leave your glasses in the tray there.

22:20.400 --> 22:26.540
When I'm twenty, you'll be twenty.
When I'm forty, you'll be forty.

22:26.540 --> 22:32.500
And when I'm 100,
I'll meet you when you're 100.

22:43.960 --> 22:50.060
Hello. I'm Alice.
I'm here to look after you.

22:50.060 --> 22:53.530
There's nothing to be afraid of.

22:53.530 --> 22:57.200
Relax and count with me.

22:57.200 --> 23:00.710
One. Two. Three.

23:00.710 --> 23:05.310
Four. Five. Six. Seven.

23:05.310 --> 23:11.720
Good night, ID code
KHM050, Kasumi Ishiki.

23:11.720 --> 23:13.810
Pleasant dreams.

23:37.240 --> 23:39.810
Please, Shizuku!

23:39.810 --> 23:43.110
Live, Kasumi!

24:06.140 --> 24:08.000
Ouch!

24:11.340 --> 24:14.010
Huh?! What is this?!

25:01.360 --> 25:03.200
Huh?

25:03.200 --> 25:04.500
Hey, what's going on?

25:04.500 --> 25:06.570
They found a cure!

25:06.570 --> 25:08.540
- They did?!
- Oww!

25:08.540 --> 25:12.040
- What is this doing here?
- What are they, weeds? Vines?

25:12.040 --> 25:14.010
Be careful! They have thorns!

25:14.010 --> 25:16.280
What in the world is going on?!

25:16.280 --> 25:18.870
What year is it?!

25:19.580 --> 25:21.010
How many years have passed?!

25:21.010 --> 25:23.510
How the hell should I know?!

25:28.220 --> 25:30.360
Hello?! Hello?!

25:30.360 --> 25:33.130
Where's the Venus Gate staff?!

25:33.130 --> 25:35.960
Hey! Someone's lying
on the ground here!

25:35.960 --> 25:38.430
Hey! You all right?!

25:39.930 --> 25:42.600
Hey! Hey!

26:12.270 --> 26:13.630
What happened?!

26:13.630 --> 26:15.330
There was a bird!

26:46.030 --> 26:48.170
The elevator!

26:48.170 --> 26:50.660
Get into the elevator!

26:51.170 --> 26:53.370
The elevator!

27:13.690 --> 27:15.400
Sorry!

27:15.400 --> 27:17.560
Are you okay?

27:25.640 --> 27:28.840
- Wow!
- What are you doing, little boy?!

27:28.840 --> 27:31.540
Deathbats! They're aerial monsters!

27:31.540 --> 27:34.750
We could beat them in one hit if
we had a wide-range wind spell!

27:34.750 --> 27:37.420
Hurry up!

27:37.420 --> 27:39.320
Come on! Hurry up!

27:39.320 --> 27:41.390
This damn elevator!

27:41.390 --> 27:44.690
Calm down! Just stay calm!

27:44.690 --> 27:47.090
Everyone stay calm!

27:48.930 --> 27:51.730
Wait! Women and children first!

27:51.730 --> 27:54.870
- Out of my way!
- Don't push me!

27:54.870 --> 27:56.530
Damn!

28:19.530 --> 28:21.860
Help me!

28:32.240 --> 28:34.930
Hurry! Hurry!

28:46.650 --> 28:48.880
Stop!

28:51.590 --> 28:54.580
Open it and we die!

29:17.780 --> 29:23.290
Hey, now! Don't skip out on us, amigo!

29:23.290 --> 29:25.690
- This way, everyone!
- Hurry!

29:35.340 --> 29:39.370
That's a lot of blood...
Are you all right?

29:39.370 --> 29:43.440
Yeah. This isn't mine.

29:43.440 --> 29:46.680
So only seven survived in the end?

29:46.680 --> 29:49.350
No, approximately seven.

29:49.350 --> 29:51.790
- Just give it up.
- What?!

29:51.790 --> 29:55.050
Ugh. What are you,
student council president now?

29:55.050 --> 30:00.390
- I'm a police officer!
- Until the world ended, you mean!

30:00.390 --> 30:02.230
Just look at this situation.

30:02.230 --> 30:07.470
It'd obviously take a hell of a long
time for things to end up this way.

30:07.470 --> 30:09.840
He's right.

30:09.840 --> 30:12.140
Those monsters...

30:12.140 --> 30:13.870
I know them!

30:13.870 --> 30:16.380
They're Deathbats, Level 1 monsters!

30:16.380 --> 30:18.010
Huh?

30:18.010 --> 30:20.310
He must be talking about a video game.

30:20.310 --> 30:21.350
What nonsense.

30:21.350 --> 30:26.550
My guess is they were some sort
of creature that evolved or mutated.

30:26.550 --> 30:29.420
Hold on! Those kinds of
changes don't happen just like that!

30:29.420 --> 30:30.690
Correct.

30:30.690 --> 30:36.030
I already told you!
The world must've ended!

30:41.770 --> 30:45.170
Just how long were we asleep?

30:45.170 --> 30:50.280
Yeah! That Alice thing was supposed
to protect us at a time like this!

30:50.280 --> 30:53.250
Where are you, Alice?! Alice!

30:53.250 --> 30:56.080
Don't be stupid.
Contacting someone comes first.

30:56.080 --> 30:59.190
Yes! A phone! A telephone!

30:59.190 --> 31:01.790
Already tried.

31:01.790 --> 31:04.720
Said they won't accept a collect call.

31:04.720 --> 31:08.700
- What the hell are you thinking?!
- I was trying to help us out!

31:08.700 --> 31:10.130
Shut up, you punk!

31:10.130 --> 31:13.900
- What's your problem?!
- What's your problem?!

31:13.900 --> 31:15.800
P-Please stop it!

31:15.800 --> 31:19.860
Have you no shame, fighting in
front of a child at a time like this?!

31:22.280 --> 31:25.640
Fine, Little Miss Mother.

31:31.420 --> 31:34.890
I tried the phone too!
It was the first thing I did!

31:34.890 --> 31:37.560
But...

31:37.560 --> 31:42.760
Those monsters aren't
the only threat to us.

31:54.010 --> 31:59.650
And there's no returning
to our capsules now.

31:59.650 --> 32:00.950
So what do we do?

32:00.950 --> 32:04.350
Ain't it obvious?!
Our only option is to go up!

32:04.350 --> 32:05.620
Up?

32:05.620 --> 32:09.020
This place is underground.
Up is the only way to run.

32:09.020 --> 32:11.990
Wait! How do we know
it's safe above ground?!

32:11.990 --> 32:17.260
We don't! But we do
know it's not safe to stay here.

32:20.370 --> 32:21.940
The worm monster?!

32:21.940 --> 32:23.970
It's a Hellworm!

32:23.970 --> 32:26.140
- Let's go up!
- Who put you in charge?!

32:26.140 --> 32:30.140
H-Hold on! I'm not going!
I'm staying right here!

32:30.140 --> 32:33.110
- Suit yourself.
- Huh?! You can't be serious!

32:33.110 --> 32:36.820
There's always a chance the geezer
will survive while we end up dead.

32:36.820 --> 32:38.450
And just the opposite, too...

32:38.450 --> 32:40.320
I'm not some geezer!

32:40.320 --> 32:44.790
I'm Senator Alessandro Peccino
from the Italian Republic!

32:44.790 --> 32:47.190
Wait! I really think we
should stick together!

32:47.190 --> 32:50.800
He says he wants to stay.

32:50.800 --> 32:56.060
No! I don't want to leave
any more people behind!

32:58.710 --> 33:01.230
She's right.

33:03.310 --> 33:07.250
Say... Weren't you one of the
twins on the same bus as me?

33:09.880 --> 33:11.680
What happened to the other one?

33:11.680 --> 33:17.890
Shizuku only accompanied me here. So...

33:17.890 --> 33:20.330
Ugh, I'm getting sick of this!

33:20.330 --> 33:25.670
Let's just go up and see
what happened to the world!

33:25.670 --> 33:27.200
See what happened?

33:27.200 --> 33:31.190
Like what's happened
to our loved ones...

33:32.440 --> 33:34.170
Let's go!

33:34.170 --> 33:37.740
- Okay, Mr. Senator.
- Let's go!

33:37.740 --> 33:39.780
I said I'm not going!

33:39.780 --> 33:43.080
How am I supposed to walk anyway?!

33:45.620 --> 33:47.890
Wh-What is this for?!

33:47.890 --> 33:50.220
Wrap your feet like this.

33:50.220 --> 33:54.560
Slow us down
and you'll get left behind.

33:57.700 --> 34:01.190
I'm serious...
you will get left behind.

34:01.930 --> 34:08.040
Once the princess fell asleep,
the king, the queen, the royal subjects,

34:08.040 --> 34:13.580
and even the dogs and birds
and fish from the garden...

34:13.580 --> 34:19.710
...dissolved into the
world of a deep dream.
- W-Wait for me!

34:30.160 --> 34:36.470
Suddenly, large, thorny
brambles wrapped around the castle

34:36.470 --> 34:42.680
and completely covered it like
a forest that had always stood there.

34:42.680 --> 34:46.270
Have I met them somewhere before?

34:47.280 --> 34:50.350
Hey! Are you sure
this is the right way?

34:50.350 --> 34:55.250
I once designed
a plant similar to this one.

34:56.990 --> 34:59.530
Well, Mr. Engineer?

34:59.530 --> 35:00.460
What is this?

35:00.460 --> 35:05.990
The tank that coverts seawater
into coolant water must've broken.

35:07.200 --> 35:11.770
Damn Venus Gate! I didn't pay all
that money just to go through this!

35:11.770 --> 35:15.510
Unbelievable. You paid your way in?

35:15.510 --> 35:19.380
I simply exercised my
rights as an important figure.

35:19.380 --> 35:21.180
Quiet!

35:21.180 --> 35:23.180
Damn! I'm gonna sue Venus Gate

35:23.180 --> 35:26.850
if anything's happened
to the fortune I saved up!

35:26.850 --> 35:31.380
- Be quiet!
- Shut up! Don't tell me what to do!

35:52.010 --> 35:53.580
No!

35:53.580 --> 35:55.680
- Don't run!
- What?!

35:55.680 --> 35:57.920
It reacts to sound!

35:57.920 --> 36:01.090
- How do you know that?!
- It's a Level 5 Demonsaurus!

36:01.090 --> 36:03.820
Games again?!

36:03.820 --> 36:08.590
He's practically blind,
so he relies entirely on his ears!

36:08.590 --> 36:13.030
- You're sure?!
- I know my data!

36:21.240 --> 36:22.210
Little boy!

36:22.210 --> 36:24.730
What are you doing?!

36:26.180 --> 36:28.270
Everyone jump in!

36:41.190 --> 36:43.860
Little boy! Little boy!

36:52.610 --> 36:55.110
Damn, that was crazy...

36:55.110 --> 36:57.280
Why isn't it coming after us?

36:57.280 --> 37:01.450
I told you, he'll only
respond to sound!

37:01.450 --> 37:03.940
Okay, okay...

37:09.160 --> 37:11.060
- Which way now?!
- This way!

37:11.060 --> 37:15.560
There's a security office this way.
Let's take cover in there for now.

37:15.560 --> 37:18.890
Wait, that girl isn't here!

37:20.070 --> 37:22.400
That slowpoke!

37:46.630 --> 37:50.790
Live... Kasumi...

38:01.840 --> 38:04.040
Oh, here they come!

38:05.650 --> 38:09.780
Damn it! I'm leaving
you behind next time!

38:09.780 --> 38:11.350
Sorry...

38:11.350 --> 38:13.890
- Now let's get the hell outta here.
- Wait!

38:13.890 --> 38:16.890
- What?!
- There should be more.

38:16.890 --> 38:19.660
- Did they kill everyone here?
- Dunno.

38:19.660 --> 38:21.390
Then don't take charge!

38:21.390 --> 38:25.350
- Shut up!
- What are you so irritated about?!

38:32.240 --> 38:35.040
R-Run!

39:08.340 --> 39:15.350
Get down!

39:15.350 --> 39:17.510
Give me a gun too!

39:21.550 --> 39:23.020
Hurry!

39:31.630 --> 39:33.290
Hurry!

39:34.400 --> 39:36.460
Get it!

39:37.600 --> 39:39.730
Get down!

39:47.410 --> 39:49.920
Not bad!

39:49.920 --> 39:51.440
Hey!

39:55.820 --> 39:57.580
Bastard!

40:06.630 --> 40:09.300
All right! We beat Stage 2!

40:09.300 --> 40:12.070
He's no ordinary guy...

40:26.320 --> 40:29.590
It petrified?! It had the Medousa virus?!

40:29.590 --> 40:33.360
That can't be! I thought
it only infected humans?

40:33.360 --> 40:35.630
A mutation, huh...

40:35.630 --> 40:37.630
I can imagine that
the virus might've mutated

40:37.630 --> 40:41.300
during the time it would've taken
for these things to come about.

40:41.300 --> 40:43.470
So it's really been that long?

40:43.470 --> 40:46.510
That, or something infected
with Medousa mutated

40:46.510 --> 40:48.640
and carried on some of its characteristics.

40:48.640 --> 40:50.970
Like what?!

40:51.440 --> 40:53.440
Something...

40:54.980 --> 40:58.950
You have a couple of ribs that
are either broken or cracked.

40:58.950 --> 41:02.350
- Class 3 damage!
- Stop that.

41:02.350 --> 41:06.230
- Where'd you get this scar?
- A long time ago.

41:06.230 --> 41:10.030
All done. Don't push yourself too hard;
this is only a temporary fix.

41:10.030 --> 41:11.460
Wow, I'm impressed.

41:11.460 --> 41:14.670
Three points of damage!
But no hindrance to the adventure!

41:14.670 --> 41:16.740
Knock that off.

41:16.740 --> 41:21.900
Well, I was a nurse before.
Until the world ended, anyway.

41:25.850 --> 41:28.380
How's it going?

41:28.380 --> 41:32.850
No luck. All that shows
up is energy-related data.

41:32.850 --> 41:35.320
Same here.

41:36.160 --> 41:40.160
Losing a party member
was a serious blow, though.

41:40.160 --> 41:41.160
Cut it out!

41:41.160 --> 41:43.730
Merchants aren't very
good in battle, though.

41:43.730 --> 41:45.730
Knock it off!

41:45.730 --> 41:49.240
I hope we'll be able to buy
weapons after we save enough gold...

41:49.240 --> 41:51.540
That's enough!

41:51.540 --> 41:55.410
This isn't a game!
People are really dying!

41:55.410 --> 41:58.610
I'm sorry. I...

41:58.610 --> 42:02.110
- That look! I can't stand that look!
- Hey, now...

42:02.110 --> 42:06.450
I could never stand that innocent,
trusting look of his!

42:06.450 --> 42:09.290
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

42:09.290 --> 42:12.730
I won't play anymore! Don't hit me!

42:12.730 --> 42:14.450
Hey!

42:17.360 --> 42:20.900
I'm sorry... I'm sorry!

42:20.900 --> 42:25.440
Geez. It's like everyone
here's got their own trauma.

42:25.440 --> 42:28.810
Is this really just a coincidence?

42:28.810 --> 42:31.310
Is it, amigo?!

42:31.310 --> 42:32.750
Why are you asking me?

42:32.750 --> 42:36.650
Because you're not a patient!

42:38.550 --> 42:40.890
Wh-What makes you think that?

42:40.890 --> 42:43.490
Your pendant!

42:43.490 --> 42:46.490
Personal belongings weren't
allowed inside the capsules.

42:46.490 --> 42:48.330
I snuck it in with me.

42:48.330 --> 42:52.300
There was a metal detector.
I saw a couple people set it off myself.

42:52.300 --> 42:55.940
Well, actually,
I bribed an employee and...

42:55.940 --> 42:58.570
You're a terrible liar.

42:58.570 --> 43:00.610
I-It's the truth! I!

43:00.610 --> 43:05.640
Then how did you know
where this office was?!

43:05.640 --> 43:08.270
You!

43:09.320 --> 43:11.650
Don't move!

43:11.650 --> 43:14.820
You're the ones who decided to tag along!

43:14.820 --> 43:19.660
I have a noble duty to fulfill!

43:19.660 --> 43:22.930
All right! Come after me and the girl dies!

43:22.930 --> 43:26.130
We won't interfere. Just let her go.

43:26.130 --> 43:29.800
The central shaft is four blocks ahead.

43:29.800 --> 43:32.300
Take the emergency
stairs there outside!

43:32.300 --> 43:34.600
Got it?!

43:37.980 --> 43:40.170
Damn!

43:47.390 --> 43:48.720
Why?!

43:48.720 --> 43:52.990
I've met you before...

43:52.990 --> 43:57.290
Just who are you?

44:01.570 --> 44:04.070
That bastard!

44:04.070 --> 44:05.370
What now?

44:05.370 --> 44:07.570
I owe that slowpoke one!

44:07.570 --> 44:09.810
Oh?

44:09.810 --> 44:12.810
But more than anything,
it's obvious that four-eyed bastard

44:12.810 --> 44:15.650
knows something about
what's going on here!

44:15.650 --> 44:18.180
We're gonna catch him
and make him talk!

44:18.180 --> 44:20.150
All right! Let's go!

44:20.150 --> 44:21.850
Wait!

44:27.560 --> 44:31.330
It's only been 48 hours
since we entered the capsules.

44:31.330 --> 44:32.530
Impossible!

44:32.530 --> 44:36.940
How could all those weird monsters
and thorns show up in only two days?!

44:36.940 --> 44:41.000
That's what he's gonna tell us.

44:50.520 --> 44:52.750
When did that happen?

44:52.750 --> 44:55.420
Right after the cold sleep began.

44:55.420 --> 44:58.220
Just after I went to sleep...
It must've been Shizuku!

44:58.220 --> 44:59.390
Shizuku?

44:59.390 --> 45:05.800
My twin sister. So she's still alive...

45:05.800 --> 45:09.470
So what happened then?!
Where did Shizuku go?!

45:09.470 --> 45:14.800
At some point she just disappeared.
By the time I realized it...

45:20.750 --> 45:24.650
- I don't know about this!
- Shh!

45:24.650 --> 45:27.980
Damn. This isn't good.

45:33.390 --> 45:35.630
- What do we do?
- We climb.

45:35.630 --> 45:37.800
I can't believe this!

45:37.800 --> 45:38.960
Can you do it?

45:38.960 --> 45:43.490
There was a dungeon set up
just like this! The Labyrinth Tower!

45:54.750 --> 45:56.650
- All right.
- You're next.

45:56.650 --> 45:59.790
What?!

45:59.790 --> 46:01.290
What are you thinking?!

46:01.290 --> 46:04.150
You have something you have to do.

46:05.820 --> 46:08.920
I'm gonna kick your
ass once we're outside.

46:14.600 --> 46:17.870
You gotta be kidding me!

46:17.870 --> 46:19.610
Don't let go, no matter what.

46:19.610 --> 46:24.680
Be careful! The Labyrinth Tower
has a lot of hidden traps!

46:24.680 --> 46:27.940
This is no time for that nonsense.

46:41.490 --> 46:43.360
Damn!

46:47.070 --> 46:49.230
All right, there's no other choice!

46:49.230 --> 46:52.860
- Wait! Don't tell me you're!
- Bingo!

47:00.980 --> 47:02.970
Shit!

47:13.160 --> 47:16.560
Oh, Kasumi! You came to visit me again!

47:16.560 --> 47:18.100
Yeah...

47:18.100 --> 47:23.670
Look! I can already walk
without using handrails!

47:23.670 --> 47:25.740
Don't worry!

47:25.740 --> 47:29.040
I will get better!

47:29.840 --> 47:30.910
Kasumi?

47:30.910 --> 47:36.010
Shizuku... You missed
summer camp because of me...

47:36.010 --> 47:38.080
And you're even behind in school now...

47:38.080 --> 47:42.860
Oh, is that all?

47:42.860 --> 47:47.790
You can help me study everything
I missed. Then we'll be even.

47:47.790 --> 47:49.520
Okay!

47:50.530 --> 47:53.120
- Shizuku! I'm open!
- I'm open!

47:55.370 --> 47:57.700
Wow! You were great, Shizuku!

47:57.700 --> 48:01.100
I thought that shot was impossible!

48:05.280 --> 48:06.410
Why?!

48:06.410 --> 48:08.410
Why?! Why?!

48:08.410 --> 48:10.780
Why?!

48:10.780 --> 48:12.320
Stop, Kasumi.

48:12.320 --> 48:16.590
But why did we both have
to catch the same disease?!

48:16.590 --> 48:19.990
The same disease
that killed Mom and Dad!

48:19.990 --> 48:21.060
Kasumi...

48:21.060 --> 48:23.660
Why couldn't it have just been me?!

48:23.660 --> 48:26.670
Don't talk like that!

48:26.670 --> 48:31.000
We're the only family we have left.

48:31.000 --> 48:35.000
Let's get through this together, okay?

48:38.010 --> 48:41.970
Just like when we were kids.

48:44.280 --> 48:46.340
It's a promise!

49:39.140 --> 49:41.660
What is this?

49:45.840 --> 49:47.380
Oh, it's you.

49:47.380 --> 49:53.090
Sorry. I-I never imagined
something like this would happen!

49:53.090 --> 49:54.650
Calm down.

49:54.650 --> 50:00.230
It's impossible to wake a single
patient without Alice noticing.

50:00.230 --> 50:04.060
So I faked a power outage
caused by temporarily-crossed lines.

50:04.060 --> 50:08.100
But that caused something to go awry.

50:08.100 --> 50:12.040
What happened?!

50:12.040 --> 50:16.680
Thinking quickly, I put on a corpse's
clothes and pretended to be a patient.

50:16.680 --> 50:18.210
Are you serious?!

50:18.210 --> 50:22.210
I lost the memory card
with the info on it then,

50:22.210 --> 50:25.080
but look, I'm almost
finished re-copying it!

50:25.080 --> 50:28.090
I set it up so I could access
the backup files anywhere

50:28.090 --> 50:31.750
just in case something happened!

50:33.290 --> 50:38.260
Keep working, amigo. I'll go check it out.

50:38.260 --> 50:39.360
Why?

50:39.360 --> 50:41.900
Why? Why?

50:41.900 --> 50:46.360
You're wondering, "Why?"

50:52.710 --> 50:57.820
I developed the cold sleep capsules.

50:57.820 --> 51:00.720
I wanted to prove that
my theory was correct.

51:00.720 --> 51:05.490
And I thought it would be
wonderful if it could help save mankind.

51:05.490 --> 51:11.560
Of course, I'd be lying if I said
I wasn't a little eager for fame too.

51:11.560 --> 51:14.270
And the devil took advantage of that.

51:14.270 --> 51:15.900
Devil?

51:15.900 --> 51:21.640
The one acting like a king at
the top of this castle's tower.

51:25.840 --> 51:27.810
It's terrifying.

51:27.810 --> 51:33.150
I didn't realize I was helping
to betray God until it was too late!

51:39.420 --> 51:44.990
This is a revelation. Expose the truth
behind Venus Gate to the world.

51:46.930 --> 51:51.270
How? How can you say that so calmly?!

51:52.440 --> 51:55.370
- It's nothing but self-serving logic!
- That's not...

51:55.370 --> 51:57.380
You gave people halfhearted hope

51:57.380 --> 52:00.480
and wound up only
increasing their despair!

52:00.480 --> 52:02.880
If you hadn't
invented those stupid things,

52:02.880 --> 52:06.180
I wouldn't have had to leave Shizuku!

52:06.180 --> 52:09.050
I'll face the consequences for that!

52:16.330 --> 52:19.230
Take it!

52:20.400 --> 52:24.170
Whoever nears the "Knowledge
Hidden in Medousa" will be victorious!

52:24.170 --> 52:26.830
Don't forget that!

52:38.220 --> 52:40.510
You idiot!

52:43.490 --> 52:46.480
What are you doing?!

52:56.740 --> 52:59.100
Go, go, go!

53:10.450 --> 53:13.210
Liar! Liar!

53:21.460 --> 53:24.260
Shizuku!

53:49.450 --> 53:52.550
Now we're even.

53:56.460 --> 53:59.060
Time to make a deal.

53:59.060 --> 54:01.230
- Give it to me.
- No!

54:01.230 --> 54:04.640
It isn't worth risking your life over.

54:04.640 --> 54:08.160
Just who are you?!

54:11.610 --> 54:15.570
Knowing wouldn't change anything.

54:20.320 --> 54:23.080
"Laura"?

54:29.660 --> 54:35.000
Damn, you're annoying!

55:08.070 --> 55:10.300
You owe me!

55:10.300 --> 55:12.070
Huh?

55:15.210 --> 55:17.330
No way!

55:21.150 --> 55:23.910
What's with this one?!

55:26.050 --> 55:28.490
Hey! What are you..?!

55:28.490 --> 55:32.520
Damn! It wasn't like this earlier!

55:32.520 --> 55:34.360
Climb!

55:38.600 --> 55:41.590
Up! Go up!

55:43.440 --> 55:44.730
Hurry!

56:01.290 --> 56:04.360
Special cocktail!

56:04.360 --> 56:07.420
Up for a glass?

56:19.600 --> 56:23.800
Now you don't have to worry
about being chased after.

56:26.140 --> 56:27.740
Hurry!

56:48.830 --> 56:50.400
What is this place?

56:50.400 --> 56:54.070
Little boy? Little boy?!

56:57.610 --> 57:01.980
Good to see you're all right. What
happened to the guy with the necklace?

57:01.980 --> 57:05.180
- He's dead. A monster attacked him.
- Little boy!

57:05.180 --> 57:09.250
- You mean a Demonsaurus!
- There you are!

57:09.250 --> 57:11.260
Just before he died, he told me

57:11.260 --> 57:14.330
to expose the truth behind
Venus Gate to the world.

57:14.330 --> 57:16.690
But the evidence is gone now...

57:16.690 --> 57:18.600
Who was he?

57:18.600 --> 57:22.330
He's the one who can tell you that.

57:26.300 --> 57:29.010
- You idiot...
- What?!

57:29.010 --> 57:32.640
Were you planning to have
a drink and wait for help?

57:32.640 --> 57:35.310
You've trapped us in
a room with no way out.

57:35.310 --> 57:38.180
Who the hell do you think you are?!

57:38.180 --> 57:43.660
I'm Lieutenant
Marco Owen of the British SAS.

57:43.660 --> 57:46.660
I infiltrated the CSCC
pretending to be a selectee.

57:46.660 --> 57:48.660
I was to secure information with his help

57:48.660 --> 57:53.630
and assist with the facility's
destruction from the outside!

57:53.630 --> 57:55.400
Information about what?

57:55.400 --> 57:59.570
Proof that Medousa was an act of
bioterrorism perpetrated by Venus Gate,

57:59.570 --> 58:03.740
or any clues about the truth
behind the Medousa virus.

58:03.740 --> 58:07.250
Cool! It's just like True Commando!

58:07.250 --> 58:11.480
You can't be serious...
Don't suddenly talk like this is a movie...

58:11.480 --> 58:16.750
Unknown viruses and cold sleep
already sound like dreams to begin with,

58:16.750 --> 58:20.330
but what's next?!
I'd rather have this all be a dream!

58:20.330 --> 58:22.330
So you've been grinning in the shadows,

58:22.330 --> 58:25.820
watching us scurry around
while you know the whole story?!

58:33.340 --> 58:38.110
Knowing what's going on
won't change our situation.

58:38.110 --> 58:41.550
It's either turn to stone and
die or get eaten by monsters.

58:41.550 --> 58:43.210
This is all your fault.

58:43.210 --> 58:46.180
No. This situation is abnormal.

58:46.180 --> 58:49.520
- What are you going to do?
- Accomplish my mission.

58:49.520 --> 58:51.890
I'm going to capture Venus Gate's leader.

58:51.890 --> 58:52.920
Even now?!

58:52.920 --> 58:56.060
He hasn't been infected,
despite being involved

58:56.060 --> 58:58.230
since the Medousa virus appeared.

58:58.230 --> 59:00.630
He definitely knows some sort of secret.

59:00.630 --> 59:01.930
Secret?

59:01.930 --> 59:05.570
A cure for the Medousa virus.

59:05.570 --> 59:07.810
The last thing that man said was,

59:07.810 --> 59:12.440
"Whoever nears the knowledge
hidden in Medousa will be victorious!"

59:15.980 --> 59:19.310
- Monsters again?!
- No! It's an earthquake!

59:25.990 --> 59:27.750
The doors!

59:34.500 --> 59:36.660
A monster!

59:37.000 --> 59:41.440
- One of those damn lizards again?!
- You mean Demonsaurus!

59:41.440 --> 59:44.140
Let it in! I'll blow it away!

59:44.140 --> 59:46.610
Wait! I think it's...

59:46.610 --> 59:48.080
It's what?!

59:48.080 --> 59:51.450
I think it might be a person!

59:56.320 --> 59:58.360
It's!

59:58.360 --> 01:00:01.330
Mr. Vega!

01:00:01.330 --> 01:00:03.460
D-Don't shoot...

01:00:03.460 --> 01:00:05.620
Please don't shoot...

01:00:09.030 --> 01:00:10.760
Stop!

01:00:13.040 --> 01:00:14.840
Mr. Owen!

01:00:14.840 --> 01:00:17.540
That's Marco!

01:00:17.540 --> 01:00:19.530
Are you okay?!

01:00:24.150 --> 01:00:27.120
What happened?
What's going on outside?

01:00:27.120 --> 01:00:29.490
The test subject went berserk.

01:00:29.490 --> 01:00:34.690
She's out of my control now.
No, she's gone beyond my reach...

01:00:34.690 --> 01:00:37.700
You were running an experiment?
What kind?!

01:00:37.700 --> 01:00:42.470
An experiment to turn dreams
into reality, I suppose you could say.

01:00:42.470 --> 01:00:46.740
I was one step away,
when something interfered...

01:00:46.740 --> 01:00:48.400
It's a big one!

01:00:53.180 --> 01:00:55.740
The coolant water's reached here?!

01:00:56.710 --> 01:00:59.650
- This is!
- It's seawater!

01:01:09.530 --> 01:01:11.500
Come on!

01:01:14.200 --> 01:01:17.370
You didn't flee into
this room by coincidence.

01:01:17.370 --> 01:01:20.670
You came here for a reason.

01:01:44.130 --> 01:01:46.130
It's the final dungeon!

01:01:46.130 --> 01:01:50.130
Is this way out real or a dream?

01:01:50.130 --> 01:01:53.630
You first. And don't try anything funny.

01:01:59.780 --> 01:02:02.770
It happened eight years ago.

01:02:04.580 --> 01:02:08.620
Immediately after, a nearby village
was wiped out by a mysterious illness.

01:02:08.620 --> 01:02:10.660
Except for one little girl.

01:02:10.660 --> 01:02:14.990
Medousa! The Medousa
virus came from space?

01:02:14.990 --> 01:02:17.560
That, at least, was
a possibility we expected.

01:02:17.560 --> 01:02:21.500
The issue was the UMA that appeared
in the village at nearly the same time.

01:02:21.500 --> 01:02:23.400
UMA?

01:02:31.240 --> 01:02:36.310
After a fierce battle, my men
were able to silence the creature.

01:02:39.450 --> 01:02:42.520
Larrue!

01:02:42.520 --> 01:02:45.520
This creature was far more bizarre

01:02:45.520 --> 01:02:48.660
than anything that had
ever existed on Earth.

01:02:48.660 --> 01:02:50.800
Bizarre, how?

01:02:50.800 --> 01:02:56.700
Simply put, it was as if it had been
born from fiction. It was nonsense.

01:02:56.700 --> 01:02:58.700
As I continued investigating, I determined

01:02:58.700 --> 01:03:02.970
that it had been born from
the little girl's imagination.

01:03:10.450 --> 01:03:13.350
A dream? You're saying
a dream became reality?!

01:03:13.350 --> 01:03:18.120
More precisely, something served
as a catalyst to manifest her fantasy.

01:03:18.120 --> 01:03:20.960
Wait, you don't mean?

01:03:20.960 --> 01:03:25.450
The mysterious disease, the girl,
and the UMA were all connected.

01:03:27.060 --> 01:03:29.470
The girl was infected
with the Medousa virus,

01:03:29.470 --> 01:03:35.070
but she conquered it by
producing an "Alternative."

01:03:35.070 --> 01:03:39.580
It turns out Medousa existed in
space long before mankind was born.

01:03:39.580 --> 01:03:42.980
It interferes with beings that
possess advanced mental activity

01:03:42.980 --> 01:03:45.180
and stimulates their evolution.

01:03:45.180 --> 01:03:46.650
You mean?

01:03:46.650 --> 01:03:50.490
But I was the one and only
person in the world who realized it.

01:03:50.490 --> 01:03:55.430
Why?! It's worthy of being
called a heavenly revelation!

01:03:55.430 --> 01:03:58.730
Why did life evolve?

01:03:58.730 --> 01:04:04.270
Because it wished to evolve.
Because it could imagine being evolved.

01:04:04.270 --> 01:04:08.510
Our fate was decided the moment
the Medousa virus came to this planet.

01:04:08.510 --> 01:04:13.610
No one can escape it.
It is an ordeal imposed upon us!

01:04:13.610 --> 01:04:17.050
Mankind is ignorantly at its mercy.

01:04:17.050 --> 01:04:20.620
I decided to try controlling it.

01:04:20.620 --> 01:04:22.620
Human consciousness is full of noise,

01:04:22.620 --> 01:04:26.290
being constantly
bombarded by external stimuli.

01:04:26.290 --> 01:04:31.920
Collecting our thoughts with
willpower alone is near impossible.

01:04:43.880 --> 01:04:49.650
A concentrated explosion of emotion
coupled with the loss of rational thought

01:04:49.650 --> 01:04:56.110
is the only way we can remain
immersed in the world of imagination.

01:04:57.760 --> 01:05:00.420
I feel very sorry for Alice...

01:05:00.420 --> 01:05:05.130
She took my hand without
hesitation when I extended it.

01:05:05.130 --> 01:05:08.230
She endured one grueling
experiment after another

01:05:08.230 --> 01:05:10.940
without even a single complaint...

01:05:10.940 --> 01:05:14.300
Why wasn't I able
to imagine how she felt?

01:05:21.910 --> 01:05:26.150
I wanted to requite
the sacrifice she had made.

01:05:32.860 --> 01:05:36.590
I decided to make one final gamble.

01:05:36.590 --> 01:05:38.800
He's gone!

01:05:38.800 --> 01:05:44.040
In short, I gathered the most promising
test subjects from around the world

01:05:44.040 --> 01:05:46.300
to dramatically drive evolution forward.

01:05:46.300 --> 01:05:48.210
The cold sleep center!

01:05:48.210 --> 01:05:51.840
You said even dreams can
be controlled during cold sleep...

01:05:51.840 --> 01:05:57.180
But then those fools just had to interfere...

01:05:57.180 --> 01:05:59.480
Powerful countries are always the same!

01:05:59.480 --> 01:06:02.490
They never hesitate
to ignore their own foolishness

01:06:02.490 --> 01:06:07.480
and steal others' work as
if it's their legitimate right!

01:06:13.060 --> 01:06:16.700
It happened just after the cold
sleep capsules were activated.

01:06:16.700 --> 01:06:19.300
A girl was brought to the lab.

01:06:19.300 --> 01:06:23.410
Such irony... Such dumb luck...

01:06:23.410 --> 01:06:26.680
This girl, who hadn't
even been on the list,

01:06:26.680 --> 01:06:31.520
was the second perfect conformant
I had worked so hard to find!

01:06:31.520 --> 01:06:33.810
You don't mean?!

01:06:36.220 --> 01:06:39.220
She was producing
tremendous amounts of energy.

01:06:39.220 --> 01:06:43.360
Something had triggered her
mind into running out of control.

01:06:43.360 --> 01:06:47.320
Just what sort of emotion
could have caused that?!

01:06:56.710 --> 01:06:59.840
- What happened?!
- Alice was knocked offline!

01:06:59.840 --> 01:07:01.710
Determine the cause!

01:07:08.720 --> 01:07:14.020
Freed from Alice's mental restraints,
she ran out of control!

01:07:16.290 --> 01:07:18.560
Even with Alice offline,

01:07:18.560 --> 01:07:22.870
cutting the main power should have
stopped the conformant's rampage!

01:07:22.870 --> 01:07:27.070
Why didn't you?! You had the ability to!

01:07:29.270 --> 01:07:31.910
Because I couldn't...

01:07:31.910 --> 01:07:35.610
After Alice,
I'd experienced failure after failure.

01:07:35.610 --> 01:07:41.110
But, at last, I had found the
greatest research subject!

01:07:42.550 --> 01:07:48.290
Alternatives produced by
conformants are immune to Medousa.

01:07:48.290 --> 01:07:52.260
They aren't immortal, but they
have essentially permanent lifespans.

01:07:52.260 --> 01:07:58.740
Remember this.
We are the beginning of everything.

01:07:58.740 --> 01:08:00.100
Yes!

01:08:00.100 --> 01:08:02.740
We have heard the voice of God!

01:08:02.740 --> 01:08:04.500
Stop!

01:08:15.190 --> 01:08:18.020
Looks like I owe you again!

01:08:18.020 --> 01:08:20.660
I won't let anyone else die!

01:08:20.660 --> 01:08:25.820
Where is this girl?! Please take me there!

01:08:35.610 --> 01:08:38.280
Little boy! Little boy!

01:08:38.280 --> 01:08:40.370
Little boy!

01:08:44.280 --> 01:08:45.650
You idiot!

01:08:55.960 --> 01:08:57.520
Little boy!

01:09:04.340 --> 01:09:06.170
Little boy!

01:09:13.680 --> 01:09:16.550
Go! It seems to like me!

01:09:16.550 --> 01:09:19.550
Doing things on your own again?!

01:09:19.550 --> 01:09:22.990
Go! Only that kid knows the way out now!

01:09:22.990 --> 01:09:24.920
Let's go!

01:09:24.920 --> 01:09:26.390
Mr. Owen!

01:09:26.390 --> 01:09:28.360
It's Marco!

01:09:37.840 --> 01:09:39.200
What's the matter?!

01:09:39.200 --> 01:09:46.110
Your prince won't invite you to
dance if that's the best you can do!

01:09:49.550 --> 01:09:51.740
Goodbye, darling!

01:10:16.410 --> 01:10:20.210
I'm sorry... Laura...

01:10:30.290 --> 01:10:31.390
You're!

01:10:31.390 --> 01:10:34.790
I decided I won't abandon anyone else!

01:10:34.790 --> 01:10:37.780
I won't turn my back anymore...

01:10:41.470 --> 01:10:46.060
All right. I still do owe her and all!

01:11:04.360 --> 01:11:06.080
Little boy!

01:11:07.190 --> 01:11:08.130
Little boy!

01:11:08.130 --> 01:11:11.960
I'm sorry! I won't hit you anymore!
Don't leave Mommy alone!

01:11:11.960 --> 01:11:16.260
God! Please don't take my child from me!

01:11:31.820 --> 01:11:33.370
Little boy!

01:11:42.490 --> 01:11:44.330
Mr. Owen!

01:11:44.330 --> 01:11:46.300
Call me Marco!

01:11:47.360 --> 01:11:49.530
Where is he? What happened to him?!

01:11:49.530 --> 01:11:52.840
Police Sergeant Ron Portman
fell in the line of duty.

01:11:52.840 --> 01:11:57.370
What's the matter? Was there an
accident along your planned route...

01:11:57.370 --> 01:11:59.500
...Alice?

01:12:01.350 --> 01:12:05.320
You brainwashed the kid
during cold sleep, didn't you?

01:12:05.320 --> 01:12:08.720
- Why are you helping us?
- You can't be serious...

01:12:08.720 --> 01:12:10.720
He was taught in his sleep.

01:12:10.720 --> 01:12:15.590
It is my duty to protect
the lives of the Sleepers...

01:12:15.590 --> 01:12:16.860
Little boy!

01:12:16.860 --> 01:12:19.100
- Huh?
- Little boy!

01:12:19.100 --> 01:12:21.100
His hypnosis was lifted.

01:12:21.100 --> 01:12:22.270
But...

01:12:22.270 --> 01:12:27.260
What was it for? Why him?

01:12:29.240 --> 01:12:31.610
At this rate...

01:12:34.010 --> 01:12:35.550
- Jump in.
- You can't be serious!

01:12:35.550 --> 01:12:38.380
Once you're in, swim back up!

01:12:38.380 --> 01:12:41.420
Grab on to something that's floating!
Anything will do!

01:12:41.420 --> 01:12:43.020
Hold on!

01:12:43.020 --> 01:12:47.090
- Can you do it, Tim?
- Don't worry! I'll be a warrior!

01:12:47.090 --> 01:12:49.690
Tim? Your name is Tim?

01:12:49.690 --> 01:12:52.460
Yeah! It's Timothy, actually.

01:12:52.460 --> 01:12:55.870
I'm gonna become a warrior
and get my parents back together!

01:12:55.870 --> 01:12:58.200
You heard the man!

01:13:00.700 --> 01:13:01.810
Five!

01:13:01.810 --> 01:13:02.740
Four!

01:13:02.740 --> 01:13:03.910
Three!

01:13:03.910 --> 01:13:05.110
Two!

01:13:05.110 --> 01:13:06.080
One!

01:13:06.080 --> 01:13:07.870
Go!

01:13:24.800 --> 01:13:28.230
- Turner! Look after Tim!
- Tim!

01:13:32.670 --> 01:13:35.000
Shizuku...

01:13:37.110 --> 01:13:38.510
You idiot!

01:13:38.510 --> 01:13:41.100
What are you doing?!

01:13:43.680 --> 01:13:48.780
If I die, you can use my capsule...

01:13:51.860 --> 01:13:54.990
Even Mom and Dad used to mix us up.

01:13:54.990 --> 01:13:57.690
I don't want you to have
to be my substitute anymore!

01:13:57.690 --> 01:13:58.830
Substitute?

01:13:58.830 --> 01:14:03.430
Even that accident in
grade school was because...

01:14:03.430 --> 01:14:04.540
Don't be stupid!

01:14:04.540 --> 01:14:07.670
You're still concerned about that?!

01:14:07.670 --> 01:14:10.470
You idiot!

01:14:10.470 --> 01:14:13.840
You can be such an idiot, Kasumi...

01:14:13.840 --> 01:14:17.010
Don't worry. I'm sure
we'll see each other again.

01:14:17.010 --> 01:14:18.680
But...

01:14:18.680 --> 01:14:20.980
People are actually pretty surprising!

01:14:20.980 --> 01:14:24.460
If we wish hard enough,
I'm sure it'll come true!

01:14:24.460 --> 01:14:27.690
Miracles only happen
where there's a wish!

01:14:27.690 --> 01:14:29.830
Don't you agree?

01:14:29.830 --> 01:14:33.860
I'm sorry!

01:14:33.860 --> 01:14:36.300
I'm sorry...

01:14:37.840 --> 01:14:39.840
Owen!

01:14:39.840 --> 01:14:42.040
Owen! Are you all right?!

01:14:42.040 --> 01:14:44.870
Yeah! We're okay!

01:14:53.480 --> 01:14:55.920
There's a ladder! Go!

01:14:55.920 --> 01:14:57.480
Hurry!

01:15:25.250 --> 01:15:28.220
Everyone all right?!

01:15:30.250 --> 01:15:32.790
I-I am. Tim?

01:15:32.790 --> 01:15:37.290
I'm okay, Big Sis!

01:15:37.290 --> 01:15:39.130
"Auntie" would be just fine.

01:15:39.130 --> 01:15:41.720
I'm okay, Auntie!

01:15:52.040 --> 01:15:53.580
What is that?

01:15:53.580 --> 01:15:57.640
It's just like the City of Ruins
past the Undersea Continent!

01:16:16.400 --> 01:16:23.640
Many princes from many kingdoms
came to save Sleeping Beauty.

01:16:23.640 --> 01:16:26.340
However, the forest of
thorns was very deep,

01:16:26.340 --> 01:16:31.110
and every last prince who
came to save her eventually died,

01:16:31.110 --> 01:16:34.410
swallowed by those thorns.

01:16:36.190 --> 01:16:39.290
We can't escape this nightmare!

01:16:39.290 --> 01:16:42.860
It'll chase us wherever
we go and eventually kill us!

01:16:42.860 --> 01:16:45.300
You understand, don't you?!

01:16:45.300 --> 01:16:49.200
This fairytale's coming
to a permanent end too...

01:16:49.200 --> 01:16:52.300
The rest of the story...

01:16:52.300 --> 01:16:56.510
You were never able to tell
the rest to your child, were you?

01:16:56.510 --> 01:16:58.200
No...

01:17:07.880 --> 01:17:10.440
Shizuku...

01:17:13.120 --> 01:17:14.280
Hey!

01:17:20.660 --> 01:17:26.840
If that girl's dream really has become real,

01:17:26.840 --> 01:17:32.330
then just what sort of
emotion could've created this?

01:17:37.810 --> 01:17:42.050
Miracles only happen where there's a wish.

01:17:56.500 --> 01:18:01.170
- Will it fly?
- Fifty-fifty chance, I'd say.

01:18:01.170 --> 01:18:05.340
- BNN News! What happened here?!
- Get back! Get back!

01:18:05.340 --> 01:18:07.940
- They want her in the High-end Lab.
- High-end Lab?

01:18:07.940 --> 01:18:10.180
Level 0. The top of the tower.

01:18:10.180 --> 01:18:12.050
Hey! Stop that!

01:18:12.050 --> 01:18:13.610
Stop it!

01:18:18.190 --> 01:18:20.060
Girl!

01:18:20.060 --> 01:18:23.250
Help! She's!

01:18:24.230 --> 01:18:25.930
That idiot!

01:18:25.930 --> 01:18:28.200
You idiot! What are you doing?!

01:18:28.200 --> 01:18:31.930
It's Shizuku! She's!

01:18:34.810 --> 01:18:38.240
Stop, Kasumi Ishiki!

01:18:40.780 --> 01:18:45.450
I memorized the
patient list before I snuck in!

01:18:45.450 --> 01:18:48.450
Shizuku's inside the castle!

01:18:48.450 --> 01:18:51.090
She's no longer the sister you knew!

01:18:51.090 --> 01:18:55.390
I know that! I think...

01:19:03.470 --> 01:19:05.440
Kasumi!

01:19:05.440 --> 01:19:09.000
Jump! Jump across!

01:19:10.610 --> 01:19:13.100
You idiot! Come back!

01:19:19.420 --> 01:19:21.510
Damn it!

01:19:36.600 --> 01:19:38.640
Oh, so it does work!

01:19:38.640 --> 01:19:42.310
I told you the only way to know was to try!

01:19:42.310 --> 01:19:45.010
Oh, no! The castle!

01:19:45.010 --> 01:19:47.810
Shizuku!

01:20:00.720 --> 01:20:02.820
Fly!

01:20:06.900 --> 01:20:08.570
All right! Let's go!

01:20:08.570 --> 01:20:11.640
No, we're not going that way.

01:20:11.640 --> 01:20:12.640
What are you?

01:20:12.640 --> 01:20:15.710
Take me and Tim as far away as possible.

01:20:15.710 --> 01:20:17.870
It won't matter where you run to.

01:20:17.870 --> 01:20:21.910
No, I'm okay, Auntie! Just stop it!

01:20:21.910 --> 01:20:23.810
My son was taken from me,

01:20:23.810 --> 01:20:26.980
but I thought I might get to see
him again if I could stay alive!

01:20:26.980 --> 01:20:30.590
- That's the whole reason I came here!
- But it was an impossible dream!

01:20:30.590 --> 01:20:33.320
No! Tim is real, at the very least!

01:20:33.320 --> 01:20:37.860
I've decided to use what
life I have left to help him!

01:20:37.860 --> 01:20:39.690
Auntie...

01:20:46.770 --> 01:20:50.370
- Wings?!
- Not just wings!

01:20:50.370 --> 01:20:54.240
Does it intend to cover
the entire world in thorns?!

01:20:54.240 --> 01:20:56.540
It's the King of Thorns!

01:21:02.290 --> 01:21:04.620
Shizuku!

01:21:12.730 --> 01:21:16.100
Did Sleeping Beauty even
want to wake up in the first place?

01:21:16.100 --> 01:21:17.470
What do you mean?

01:21:17.470 --> 01:21:22.370
Maybe she would've been
happier if she had stayed asleep?

01:21:22.370 --> 01:21:27.640
The thorns trapped the princess,
but conversely they also kept her safe.

01:21:27.640 --> 01:21:32.320
She wouldn't age, and she could
always meet princes in her dreams.

01:21:32.320 --> 01:21:36.450
I wonder what the princess
wished for and what she dreamed of...

01:21:36.450 --> 01:21:40.560
My guess is she wished for
her dream to continue forever.

01:21:40.560 --> 01:21:42.590
Stop this!

01:21:42.590 --> 01:21:45.100
Inside a dream,
she would never be hurt

01:21:45.100 --> 01:21:47.430
and she could reset things
as often as she wanted.

01:21:47.430 --> 01:21:49.970
Is there anything
better than that in reality?

01:21:49.970 --> 01:21:53.240
Especially if she was face-to-face
with an excruciating situation.

01:21:53.240 --> 01:21:56.760
Shizuku... Let's go home!

01:22:06.850 --> 01:22:09.920
Dreams are always betrayed by reality.

01:22:09.920 --> 01:22:11.790
The prince is no exception.

01:22:11.790 --> 01:22:14.420
He might be able to lift the curse,

01:22:14.420 --> 01:22:17.430
but he can't guarantee
her future happiness.

01:22:17.430 --> 01:22:20.430
A prince inside a dream can
be reworked over and over,

01:22:20.430 --> 01:22:23.030
but the real-life prince
is like an otherworldly being.

01:22:23.030 --> 01:22:27.270
Yes. The real-life prince would...

01:22:31.310 --> 01:22:33.170
Auntie?!

01:22:42.790 --> 01:22:44.890
Auntie! Auntie!

01:22:44.890 --> 01:22:47.790
Tim! Don't let go of Mrs. Turner!

01:22:47.790 --> 01:22:53.230
- Mrs. Turner?
- Yes! She's Mrs. Katherine Turner!

01:22:53.230 --> 01:22:55.290
Marco!

01:23:24.160 --> 01:23:25.330
Shit!

01:23:25.330 --> 01:23:26.600
Mr. Owen?!

01:23:26.600 --> 01:23:29.770
Marco, damn it...

01:23:29.770 --> 01:23:34.870
- Where's Tim?! And...
- Katherine Turner.

01:23:34.870 --> 01:23:36.440
I'm pathetic.

01:23:36.440 --> 01:23:40.940
I joined the army thinking I could
do something other people couldn't,

01:23:40.940 --> 01:23:45.450
but in the end I've learned that
I'm completely helpless to do anything.

01:23:45.450 --> 01:23:50.720
- Please help me!
- Sure.

01:23:50.720 --> 01:23:53.460
Level 0 is secured like a black box,

01:23:53.460 --> 01:23:57.860
so not even we could
get detailed intel on it.

01:24:02.200 --> 01:24:06.030
Looks like we're playing this one by ear...

01:24:07.570 --> 01:24:10.300
...Amiga!
- Right!

01:24:11.910 --> 01:24:13.640
Follow me!

01:24:18.310 --> 01:24:20.040
This way!

01:24:36.070 --> 01:24:39.140
Oh, no, Auntie!
We need to get out of here!

01:24:39.140 --> 01:24:41.600
Auntie!

01:24:42.670 --> 01:24:45.300
Auntie?

01:24:46.480 --> 01:24:51.980
Then came a young and brave prince.

01:24:51.980 --> 01:24:53.650
As the prince entered the forest,

01:24:53.650 --> 01:24:57.850
the thorny brambles formed
a barrier of flowers around him,

01:24:57.850 --> 01:25:02.990
leading him further into the castle.

01:25:02.990 --> 01:25:07.000
All the dogs, birds, fish, and royal
subjects looked dead as they slept,

01:25:07.000 --> 01:25:10.330
yet never once did he flinch.

01:25:10.330 --> 01:25:17.640
Then, at last, he reached
the room where Sleeping Beauty slept.

01:25:19.280 --> 01:25:21.680
Actually, I've met you before, too.

01:25:21.680 --> 01:25:22.880
Huh?

01:25:22.880 --> 01:25:26.280
Someone wished for
this world to be a dream.

01:25:26.280 --> 01:25:27.620
What for?

01:25:27.620 --> 01:25:30.990
To protect something.
To obtain something.

01:25:30.990 --> 01:25:32.490
Shizuku...

01:25:32.490 --> 01:25:36.030
I don't know how to explain it,
but Sleeping Beauty isn't the issue;

01:25:36.030 --> 01:25:38.390
it's what she's dreaming about.

01:25:38.390 --> 01:25:42.230
Shizuku is doing this for me...

01:25:42.230 --> 01:25:44.530
I have to find out for sure.

01:25:44.530 --> 01:25:49.570
I get the feeling that only I can meet her...
That only I can stop her...

01:25:49.570 --> 01:25:51.540
All right, then! Let's go!

01:25:51.540 --> 01:25:53.200
Right!

01:26:03.390 --> 01:26:06.390
What kind of joke is this?! Or is it?

01:26:06.390 --> 01:26:08.890
Both are correct.

01:26:08.890 --> 01:26:12.930
Both are correct. Your role is now over.

01:26:12.930 --> 01:26:17.070
As you are now useless,
you will be eliminated.

01:26:17.070 --> 01:26:21.240
It's been a long time, Marco. My brother.

01:26:21.240 --> 01:26:23.540
Laura!

01:26:27.910 --> 01:26:32.720
That's the dress I gave her for
her high school graduation party!

01:26:32.720 --> 01:26:37.350
You took information from my
brain while I was asleep in the capsule!

01:26:37.350 --> 01:26:39.090
I see! I'm also!

01:26:39.090 --> 01:26:41.560
What's wrong?
Aren't you happy to see me?

01:26:41.560 --> 01:26:46.100
Alice!
Your program is malfunctioning! Repair it!

01:26:46.100 --> 01:26:50.690
No, I am running properly.

01:26:52.870 --> 01:26:56.240
Number one priority:
eliminate all unstable elements

01:26:56.240 --> 01:26:58.640
that threaten the top-level Sleeper.

01:26:58.640 --> 01:27:03.580
What does that have to do
with you brainwashing us?!

01:27:06.280 --> 01:27:11.980
"Risk your lives to protect
the small Asian girl wearing glasses."

01:27:18.660 --> 01:27:21.260
"One will be a guide."

01:27:22.230 --> 01:27:26.170
"One will protect the guide
with her maternal instincts."

01:27:26.170 --> 01:27:29.340
"One will be an expert leader
with a strong sense of justice."

01:27:29.340 --> 01:27:32.510
"One will conceal my intentions
and serve as a human shield."

01:27:32.510 --> 01:27:36.980
"And one will be a great warrior
in no danger of dying from Medousa."

01:27:36.980 --> 01:27:38.850
Marco!

01:27:40.980 --> 01:27:43.320
I was dreaming?

01:27:44.520 --> 01:27:47.660
Relax and count with me.

01:27:47.660 --> 01:27:54.460
- One. Two. Three.
- Why did I say his name?

01:27:54.460 --> 01:27:58.840
Why do you have
to protect the top-level Sleeper?!

01:27:58.840 --> 01:28:03.710
Humans who serve as hosts for the
mental parasites known as Medousa

01:28:03.710 --> 01:28:08.110
exhibit certain specific
psychological deviations.

01:28:08.110 --> 01:28:09.810
Trauma?!

01:28:09.810 --> 01:28:13.820
The more traumatized
and psychologically frail one is,

01:28:13.820 --> 01:28:17.390
the more focused that
person's mind becomes.

01:28:17.390 --> 01:28:21.360
These two things create a delicate balance.

01:28:21.360 --> 01:28:23.730
Psychologically, Kasumi's existence is vital

01:28:23.730 --> 01:28:26.960
to the stability of the top-level Sleeper.

01:28:26.960 --> 01:28:30.500
So she must be protected.

01:28:30.500 --> 01:28:34.000
Even that arrogant Italian
man had been greatly troubled

01:28:34.000 --> 01:28:37.910
by the suicide of his
corrupt younger brother.

01:28:37.910 --> 01:28:41.240
What about you, then?

01:28:44.150 --> 01:28:47.010
Hey, sorcerer!

01:29:30.690 --> 01:29:34.360
Did you lose something dear, too?

01:29:34.360 --> 01:29:38.200
Did you wish it was all a dream?

01:29:43.240 --> 01:29:45.230
Damn it!

01:29:52.620 --> 01:29:58.320
Alice can't create Alternatives.
Then what's making me see Laura?

01:29:58.320 --> 01:30:02.590
Think! Think, Marco Owen!

01:30:04.590 --> 01:30:07.000
How did she teach Tim the escape route?

01:30:07.000 --> 01:30:09.570
How did she get me to..?

01:30:09.570 --> 01:30:11.170
This is a transmitter...

01:30:11.170 --> 01:30:14.330
What else do we have in common?!

01:30:17.110 --> 01:30:19.740
That's it! That injection!

01:30:19.740 --> 01:30:24.310
Did they implant us with bio-chips?!

01:30:24.310 --> 01:30:26.920
You should've simply run away quietly.

01:30:26.920 --> 01:30:29.950
Didn't you realize that the
very act of coming back here

01:30:29.950 --> 01:30:32.960
has produced unhappiness?

01:30:32.960 --> 01:30:36.930
Sleeping Beauty was
destined to be woken in the end.

01:30:36.930 --> 01:30:39.860
That analogy goes beyond
the realm of understanding.

01:30:39.860 --> 01:30:45.270
Once people have
likened something to a story,

01:30:45.270 --> 01:30:48.640
they always follow
the comparison to the end.

01:30:48.640 --> 01:30:50.510
It's illogical.

01:30:50.510 --> 01:30:54.880
I think so too.

01:30:54.880 --> 01:30:59.150
Can you really shoot me, your own sister?

01:30:59.150 --> 01:31:03.190
The only sister I have
shattered into pieces three years ago

01:31:03.190 --> 01:31:09.490
after she jumped off a New York
building out of fear of Medousa.

01:31:11.460 --> 01:31:15.190
Goodbye, Laura...

01:31:22.910 --> 01:31:26.500
Kasumi! Kasumi!

01:31:28.410 --> 01:31:30.380
Damn, now I see...

01:31:30.380 --> 01:31:33.040
How long has?!

01:31:49.870 --> 01:31:53.940
It's impossible for you to physically
destroy me as you are now.

01:31:53.940 --> 01:31:58.410
I know. That's why I'm going
to use the "Knowledge in Medousa."

01:31:58.410 --> 01:32:02.180
If you stop me, there's no
telling what the conformant will do

01:32:02.180 --> 01:32:05.110
in her uncontrolled state.

01:32:05.110 --> 01:32:06.780
There'd be no going back.

01:32:06.780 --> 01:32:10.840
Do you want the world
to be covered in thorns?

01:32:18.090 --> 01:32:23.600
In terms of my original objective,
you might be right.

01:32:23.600 --> 01:32:31.240
But now I'm dying
to grant that idiot's wish!

01:32:31.240 --> 01:32:34.980
Stop, Lieutenant Owen!

01:32:34.980 --> 01:32:36.410
Owen!

01:32:37.080 --> 01:32:39.740
It's Marco!

01:33:06.280 --> 01:33:10.510
Did you lose something dear, too?

01:33:10.510 --> 01:33:14.510
Did you wish it was all a dream?

01:33:20.490 --> 01:33:22.460
Marco!

01:33:24.330 --> 01:33:25.800
Shizuku?!

01:33:25.800 --> 01:33:28.700
I'll always be waiting for you,

01:33:28.700 --> 01:33:33.640
so come look for me
as soon as you wake up.

01:33:33.640 --> 01:33:35.300
I'm sure we'll meet again.

01:33:35.300 --> 01:33:38.140
Miracles only happen where there's a wish.

01:33:38.140 --> 01:33:42.550
It was because of the twelfth
witch's wish that the princess survived!

01:33:42.550 --> 01:33:45.210
Wishing will make a miracle happen?

01:33:45.210 --> 01:33:48.340
Yes! It will!

01:33:52.620 --> 01:33:54.720
Kasumi?!

01:33:54.720 --> 01:33:57.160
- I've decided. I...
- Kasumi...

01:33:57.160 --> 01:33:59.630
I can't do this!

01:33:59.630 --> 01:34:06.200
I don't want to die! But I don't
want to survive and be all alone either!

01:34:06.200 --> 01:34:08.400
Kasumi?

01:34:08.400 --> 01:34:12.200
Live, Kasumi...

01:34:13.040 --> 01:34:16.480
Relax and count with me.

01:34:16.480 --> 01:34:19.080
One. Two. Three.

01:34:19.080 --> 01:34:23.050
Oh, it was just another dream...

01:34:23.050 --> 01:34:24.880
Another?

01:34:28.220 --> 01:34:30.660
This isn't a dream!

01:34:33.200 --> 01:34:36.030
M-Marco...

01:34:36.030 --> 01:34:37.900
Marco!

01:34:40.340 --> 01:34:42.530
Where am I?

01:34:44.740 --> 01:34:46.770
Marco?!

01:34:54.680 --> 01:34:56.850
Shizuku?!

01:35:04.360 --> 01:35:05.950
Shizuku!

01:35:07.400 --> 01:35:09.390
Shizuku!

01:35:24.610 --> 01:35:26.310
Shizuku?!

01:35:27.080 --> 01:35:29.790
Please. Leave me in peace.

01:35:29.790 --> 01:35:33.740
Why?! I want to help Shizuku!

01:35:38.790 --> 01:35:42.330
You're an Alternative
Shizuku's mind created!

01:35:42.330 --> 01:35:43.930
I am Shizuku.

01:35:43.930 --> 01:35:45.630
Why are you getting in the way?!

01:35:45.630 --> 01:35:47.500
I'm not in the way at all.

01:35:47.500 --> 01:35:53.740
I will remain the me you want
and you will remain the you I want.

01:35:53.740 --> 01:35:55.980
I don't understand what you're saying!

01:35:55.980 --> 01:35:59.850
You don't need to understand.

01:36:01.950 --> 01:36:04.020
Just forget about me.

01:36:04.020 --> 01:36:05.850
No!

01:36:08.460 --> 01:36:10.760
Please, stop.

01:36:10.760 --> 01:36:13.430
Absolutely not!

01:36:13.430 --> 01:36:15.160
I...

01:36:15.160 --> 01:36:16.300
Stop...

01:36:16.300 --> 01:36:19.470
I will save Shizuku!

01:36:19.470 --> 01:36:20.840
Stop!

01:36:20.840 --> 01:36:24.810
...And end this nightmare!

01:36:24.810 --> 01:36:27.500
Stop!

01:36:46.160 --> 01:36:48.150
Shizuku!

01:36:52.370 --> 01:36:55.530
Please... Stop...

01:36:59.640 --> 01:37:03.880
How did things turn out this way?!

01:37:03.880 --> 01:37:05.250
Please!

01:37:05.250 --> 01:37:10.420
If I'm... If I'm to blame, then kill me!

01:37:10.420 --> 01:37:14.190
Just don't destroy the world!

01:37:14.190 --> 01:37:16.490
Don't!

01:37:27.770 --> 01:37:31.440
Shizuku! Please! Wake up!

01:37:31.440 --> 01:37:33.680
Hear my voice!

01:37:33.680 --> 01:37:36.380
Shizuku!

01:37:36.380 --> 01:37:39.780
No! Kasumi!

01:37:43.720 --> 01:37:45.710
Shizuku!

01:37:47.690 --> 01:37:48.760
A cut...

01:37:48.760 --> 01:37:53.350
No! Don't remember!

01:38:00.470 --> 01:38:03.910
I'm... I'm...

01:38:03.910 --> 01:38:07.110
Please, Shizuku...

01:38:07.110 --> 01:38:09.110
Please! Do this with me!

01:38:09.110 --> 01:38:10.250
Kasumi!

01:38:10.250 --> 01:38:13.380
Please, Shizuku!

01:38:13.380 --> 01:38:16.450
- Stop!
- Shizuku!

01:38:16.450 --> 01:38:19.650
I said stop it!

01:38:25.790 --> 01:38:29.430
Are you all right?!

01:38:29.430 --> 01:38:31.830
- Thank you...
- Are you hurt?

01:38:31.830 --> 01:38:35.000
- Kasumi? Where's Kasumi?!
- This is GP-03. Accident occurred.

01:38:35.000 --> 01:38:39.270
- Send medical staff immediately.
- Kasumi?!

01:38:46.780 --> 01:38:52.190
N-No!

01:38:53.260 --> 01:38:57.690
- BNN News! What happened here?!
- Get back! Get back!

01:38:57.690 --> 01:38:59.930
- They want her in the High-end Lab.
- High-end Lab?

01:38:59.930 --> 01:39:02.360
Level 0. The top of the tower.

01:39:02.360 --> 01:39:04.170
Hey! Stop that!

01:39:04.170 --> 01:39:06.100
Stop it!

01:39:46.710 --> 01:39:48.140
Shizuku?!

01:39:48.140 --> 01:39:50.870
Live, Kasumi!

01:40:00.060 --> 01:40:06.260
So I'm just an
Alternative your mind created...

01:40:06.260 --> 01:40:09.060
I just wanted to change the world

01:40:09.060 --> 01:40:13.900
into one where you lived on,
without you realizing a thing...

01:40:13.900 --> 01:40:16.110
That's what I kept wishing for...

01:40:16.110 --> 01:40:20.710
I was always the one
who needed your help...

01:40:20.710 --> 01:40:24.910
No, I grew strong because
you were there for me.

01:40:24.910 --> 01:40:27.180
What should I?

01:40:27.180 --> 01:40:30.690
My wish went out of control...

01:40:30.690 --> 01:40:33.520
You'll have to live on
your own from now on.

01:40:33.520 --> 01:40:37.290
No! I'm not leaving!
I'm going to stay with you!

01:40:37.290 --> 01:40:41.860
The world will have to change
once Sleeping Beauty wakes up.

01:40:41.860 --> 01:40:43.870
No! Shizuku!

01:40:43.870 --> 01:40:46.530
Live, Kasumi...

01:41:07.260 --> 01:41:09.990
There wasn't enough
energy to run out of control?!

01:41:09.990 --> 01:41:12.150
Run! Run!

01:41:13.630 --> 01:41:15.720
It's going to self-destruct!

01:42:14.190 --> 01:42:16.830
I...

01:42:16.830 --> 01:42:20.560
I had hoped that this was all a dream.

01:42:20.560 --> 01:42:25.900
A dream I was having while
asleep inside the cold sleep capsule.

01:42:25.900 --> 01:42:29.740
I thought it would be
so nice if that were true...

01:42:29.740 --> 01:42:34.410
But it turns out I was a
dream Shizuku was having.

01:42:34.410 --> 01:42:38.850
Who knows, maybe we're all
a part of someone else's dream.

01:42:38.850 --> 01:42:40.520
Whose?

01:42:40.520 --> 01:42:45.720
A single incomprehensible
being that evolved long ago.

01:42:45.720 --> 01:42:47.820
Even if...

01:42:47.820 --> 01:42:51.430
Even if you're overcome by
unspeakable loneliness, endure it

01:42:51.430 --> 01:42:56.000
and encourage someone
who can follow where you left off.

01:42:56.000 --> 01:42:57.700
Is that?

01:42:57.700 --> 01:43:02.070
That's my final wish.

01:43:06.110 --> 01:43:08.200
Marco?

01:43:09.780 --> 01:43:12.110
Marco?!

01:43:31.230 --> 01:43:33.770
Thank you, Marco...

01:43:33.770 --> 01:43:37.470
And, goodbye...

01:43:38.570 --> 01:43:41.200
Girl!

01:43:53.460 --> 01:43:56.120
What will we do now?

01:44:06.470 --> 01:44:08.490
Hey!

01:44:10.740 --> 01:44:13.140
- Let's go.
- Where to?

01:44:13.140 --> 01:44:18.670
To somewhere where there are people.
To see your Mom and Dad.

01:44:19.980 --> 01:44:23.250
Miracles only happen where there's a wish.

01:44:23.250 --> 01:44:25.190
Right!

01:44:43.340 --> 01:44:49.880
No one knows what there is

01:44:49.880 --> 01:44:58.620
on the edge of this world
that continues forever

01:44:58.620 --> 01:45:05.530
If by some random chance
I'm able to see what's ahead

01:45:05.530 --> 01:45:13.300
then I would want to visit you

01:45:13.300 --> 01:45:18.570
I felt longing, I felt sadness,
and my love grew ever stronger

01:45:18.570 --> 01:45:24.210
Has the wish I spelled out
with sincere feelings

01:45:24.210 --> 01:45:28.650
reached you yet?

01:45:28.650 --> 01:45:34.320
I composed the fadeless
memories I dreamt of

01:45:34.320 --> 01:45:44.320
I tried to give you my heart
but time kept passing by

01:45:47.200 --> 01:45:53.540
I'm going to hold your hand tightly

01:45:53.540 --> 01:46:02.020
and rediscover your warmth

01:46:02.020 --> 01:46:08.560
Not even time
could make these wounds go away

01:46:08.560 --> 01:46:16.200
but let's put our hearts together
and heal them

01:46:16.200 --> 01:46:21.470
I'll never forget those honest eyes,
however far apart we are

01:46:21.470 --> 01:46:26.980
Has the wish I spelled out
with sincere feelings

01:46:26.980 --> 01:46:31.280
reached you yet?

01:46:31.280 --> 01:46:36.490
I want to protect you
from everything that hurts you

01:46:36.490 --> 01:46:40.290
Please make this sadness go away, God

01:46:40.290 --> 01:46:45.660
Then I'll reach the edge of this world

01:47:17.290 --> 01:47:31.170
Learning to earnestly wish
will let me live true to myself

01:47:31.170 --> 01:47:38.780
If someday I find something for someone

01:47:38.780 --> 01:47:49.320
I'll choose the path I believe in

01:47:49.890 --> 01:47:55.200
Someday I will reach the edge of this world

01:47:55.200 --> 01:48:00.540
Has the wish I spelled out
with sincere feelings

01:48:00.540 --> 01:48:04.740
reached you yet?

01:48:04.740 --> 01:48:10.250
I have faith that this wish
will bring about a miracle

01:48:10.250 --> 01:48:14.050
I will dream of eternal love

01:48:14.050 --> 01:48:19.890
until I reach the edge of this world

01:48:44.110 --> 01:48:50.350
I'll dream to the edge of this world
